        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Puneet Mishra</h1>
        <p class="deck">
          I work at the layer where the abstractions stop helping.
        </p>

        <p>
          Rust and C++ mostly, plus protocol reverse engineering, and enough
          frontend to build the tools I need. What holds it together isn't a
          language or a domain — it's an interest in what the machine is
          actually doing underneath whatever API you were handed.
        </p>

        <p>
          That means the posts here jump around: a kernel syscall one week, a
          binary wire format the next, a pathological allocation pattern after
          that. If there's a through-line, it's that most performance problems
          turn out to be someone accepting a default they never looked at.
        </p>

        <p>
          Everything on this site is written from code I've actually built and
          shipped, and the figures are live — the simulations run in your
          browser off the same logic the posts describe, not screenshots of
          something that once worked.
        </p>

        <p>
